### Steps

1. Trainer registers at `/register-trainer` → `POST /trainer/register` (creates `trainers` row).
2. Trainer signs in at `/login-trainer` → `POST /trainer/login` (JWT `role: trainer`) → `/trainer-dashboard`.
3. Overview (`/trainer-dashboard/overview`) lists all trainings for that trainer + Create CTA.
4. Trainings (`/trainer-dashboard/trainings`):
   - Create training → `POST /trainer/{id}/courses` (`trainer_id` set, `owner_id` NULL).
   - Reschedule → `POST /trainer/{id}/courses/{course_id}/reschedule` (dates/schedule + reason).
5. Club admin `/courses` flows remain unchanged (`WHERE owner_id = …`); trainer rows never appear there.

## Compatibility

| Area | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| Club courses | Still use `owner_id`; `trainer_id` stays NULL |
| Trainer courses | Use `trainer_id`; `owner_id` is NULL |
| Reschedule columns | Nullable; unused by club admin APIs |
| Club Coach role | Unchanged (`members.role = Coach`) |
